cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "tumble: a strict genetic algorithm over Go"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/scttfrdmn/tumble"
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Scott
abstract: >-
  A genetic algorithm over Go kernels that is strict in Goldberg's sense: a coded
  representation (typed linear IR), a population, blind payoff-only operators and
  probabilistic transitions, with no LLM in the loop. Fitness comes from giri, a
  UB-verifying Go SSA interpreter, whose execution traces drive a structural
  hash-cons, a Hashlife-style value cache, and a semantic fingerprint index.
keywords:
  - genetic algorithms
  - genetic programming
  - superoptimization
  - Go
  - program synthesis
references:
  - type: software
    title: "giri: Go IR interpreter for undefined-behavior detection"
    authors:
      - family-names: Friedman
        given-names: Scott
    url: "https://github.com/scttfrdmn/giri"
  - type: book
    title: "Genetic Algorithms in Search, Optimization, and Machine Learning"
    authors:
      - family-names: Goldberg
        given-names: David E.
    year: 1989
